# /imprint/ WAS A PAGE ON THIS SITE AND IS NOW A DOCUMENT SOMEWHERE ELSE.
#
# It was live, it was linked from the footer of every page, and it was in the
# sitemap for three days. Removing the route without this file turns every one
# of those into a 404 -- a bookmark, a link in a chat, a crawler holding the
# URL. Worse, the one thing a reader looking for an imprint would be sent to is
# a page saying there is none.
#
# 301 rather than 302: the move is permanent, and a permanent redirect is what
# tells a crawler to transfer the URL rather than keep checking this one.
#
# BOTH FORMS, because `/imprint` without the slash was a 307 to `/imprint/` and
# that 307 goes away with the asset. Left alone it would land on the 404 page
# instead, which is the same defect one hop earlier.

/imprint      https://legal.sw-labs.de/imprint  301
/imprint/     https://legal.sw-labs.de/imprint  301
